{
  "$comment": "Contracts 2.1.0 (cases added in 2.5.0 carry `since`): must-reject corpus for the Diplomacy press layer. Each case is a diplomacy_action frame plus the engine context it arrives in, and the required outcome. `expect.frame` = schema_invalid means the arena edge refuses the whole frame (reject reason schema_invalid, counted in budget.actions_rejected); accepted means the frame is schema-valid and the listed per-message press rejects (diplomacy_press_reject codes) must be produced, the listed message indexes delivered, and nothing else. contracts/tools/contract-check.mjs checks the schema half; the press-layer implementation test (Phase 8 B3) replays every case against the engine. Credential-shaped values contain EXAMPLE.",
